      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Prompt caching can be implicit, where Amazon Bedrock selects where the reusable prefix ends, or explicit, where your code marks that endpoint using prompt_cache_breakpoint .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/groundhog-day-for-ai-agents-prompt-caching-patterns-for-using-openai-models-on-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T17:27:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-27T15:53:36.902Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 2: Turn 1 saves the prompt prefix up to the breakpoint, and turn 2 reuses it and pays full price only for the new question",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/groundhog-day-for-ai-agents-prompt-caching-patterns-for-using-openai-models-on-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T17:27:20.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-27T15:53:36.902Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In one of our tests using explicit caching, the roughly 4,000-token tools-and-instructions prefix wrote 4,120 tokens on the first request and read those 4,120 tokens on later requests.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/groundhog-day-for-ai-agents-prompt-caching-patterns-for-using-openai-models-on-amazon-bedrock/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
